│                                              │
│ The core problem is that Django’s in_bulk()  │
│ method, when used with a field defined by a  │
│ UniqueConstraint, incorrectly identifies the │
│ field as not unique, leading to a            │
│ ValueError. This happens because in_bulk()   │
│ relies on the unique=True attribute of a     │
│ field to determine uniqueness.               │
│ UniqueConstraint defines uniqueness through  │
│ a constraint, not a boolean attribute. The   │
│ fix is to explicitly check if the field is   │
│ unique before calling in_bulk(). This        │
│ ensures that in_bulk() only operates on      │
│ fields that genuinely have a unique          │
│ constraint defined.                          │
│                                              │
│ Patch:                                       │
│                                              │
│                                              │
│  # modification 1                            │
│  [file]django/db/models/query.py[/file]      │
│  [original]                                  │
│  def in_bulk(self, fields=None,              │
│  batch_size=None, pop={"id": None}):         │
│      """                                     │
│      Updates multiple records in a database  │
│  transaction.                                │
│                                              │
│      This method is intended for bulk updat  │
│  and should be used with caution.            │
│      It is not recommended for large         │
│  datasets.                                   │
│      """                                     │
│      if fields is None:                      │
│          fields = self.get_fields()          │
│      if not fields:                          │
│          return                              │
│      if not self.exists():                   │
│          return                              │
│      if not self.base_queryset.exists():     │
│          return                              │
│                                              │
│      if not self.base_queryset.is_distinct(  │
│          raise ValueError("in_bulk()'s       │
│  field_name must be a unique field but %r    │
│  isn't." % fields)                           │
│  [/original]                                 │
