│ Okay, let’s address this issue.              │
│                                              │
│ Reasoning:                                   │
│                                              │
│ The core problem is that Django’s in_bulk()  │
│ method, when used with a field defined by a  │
│ UniqueConstraint, incorrectly throws a       │
│ ValueError. This is because in_bulk()        │
│ expects a unique field to be present, and    │
│ UniqueConstraint enforces uniqueness, not    │
│ unique=True. The fix is to allow in_bulk()   │
│ to operate on fields with UniqueConstraint   │
│ by checking if the field is actually unique  │
│ before attempting the bulk operation. We can │
│ achieve this by adding a check within the    │
│ in_bulk method to verify uniqueness.         │
│                                              │
│ Patch:                                       │
│                                              │
│                                              │
│  # modification 1                            │
│  [file]django/db/models/query.py[/file]      │
│  [original]                                  │
│  def in_bulk(self, fields=None,              │
│  batch_size=None, populator=None):           │
│      """                                     │
│      Perform bulk updates or inserts on a    │
│  QuerySet.                                   │
│                                              │
│      If fields is specified, it must be a    │
│  list of field names.                        │
│      """                                     │
│      if fields is None:                      │
│          fields = self.get_fields()          │
│      if not fields:                          │
│          return self                         │
│      if batch_size is None:                  │
│          batch_size =                        │
│  self.model.objects.get_bulk_field_count()   │
│                                              │
│      if not self.check_for_update():         │
│          raise PermissionDenied("Cannot      │
│  update objects via in_bulk")                │
│                                              │
│      if not self.exists():                   │
│          return self                         │
│                                              │
│      if fields and not all(field in          │
│  self.get_fields() for field in fields):     │
│          raise ValueError(                   │
│              "in_bulk()'s field_name must b  │
│  a unique field but %r isn't."               │
│              % ", ".join(fields)             │
│          )                                   │
│                                              │
│      # ... (rest of the in_bulk method)      │
│  [/original]                                 │
│  [patched]                                   │
│  def in_bulk(self, fields=None,              │
│  batch_size=None, populator=None):           │
│      """                                     │
│      Perform bulk updates or inserts on a    │
│  QuerySet.                                   │
│                                              │
│      If fields is specified, it must be a    │
│  list of field names.                        │
│      """                                     │
│      if fields is None:                      │
│          fields = self.get_fields()          │
│      if not fields:                          │
│          return self                         │
│      if batch_size is None:                  │
│          batch_size =                        │
│  self.model.objects.get_bulk_field_count()   │
│                                              │
│      if not self.check_for_update():         │
│          raise PermissionDenied("Cannot      │
│  update objects via in_bulk")                │
│                                              │
│      if not self.exists():                   │
│          return self                         │
│                                              │
│      if fields and not all(field in          │
│  self.get_fields() for field in fields):     │
│          raise ValueError(                   │
│              "in_bulk()'s field_name must b  │
│  a unique field but %r isn't."               │
│              % ", ".join(fields)             │
│          )                                   │
│                                              │
│      # Check if the field is unique          │
│      for field in fields:                    │
│          if not self.using_signals and not   │
│  self.model._meta.constraints.get(field):    │
│              continue                        │
│          if not                              │
│  self.model._meta.constraints.get(field):    │
│              continue                        │
│          if                                  │
│  self.model._meta.constraints[field].name !  │
│  '%(app_label)s_%(class)s_%s_unq':           │
│              continue                        │
│          if not                              │
│  self.get_value_for_update(field):           │
│              raise ValueError(               │
│                  "in_bulk()'s field_name mu  │
│  be a unique field but %r isn't."            │
│                  % field                     │
│              )                               │
│                                              │
│      # ... (rest of the in_bulk method)      │
│  [/patched]                                  │
│                                              │
│                                              │
│ Explanation of Changes:                      │
│                                              │
│ The patch adds a loop that iterates through  │
│ the specified fields. Inside the loop, it    │
│ checks if the field has a UniqueConstraint   │
│ defined. If it does, it calls                │
│ self.get_value_for_update(field) to verify   │
│ that the value of the field is unique. If    │
│ the value is not unique, a ValueError is     │
│ raised. This ensures that in_bulk() only     │
│ operates on unique fields, resolving the     │
│ original issue. The check for                │
│ self.using_signals and                       │
│ self.model._meta.constraints.get(field) is   │
│ added to handle cases where the constraint   │
│ is not directly accessible. Also, the check  │
│ for the constraint name is added to ensure   │
│ that the correct constraint is being         │
│ checked.                                     │
