│ Explanation:                                 │
│                                              │
│ The patch adds a check to ensure that if a   │
│ field has a UniqueConstraint, the            │
│ get_unique_values method is called to verify │
│ uniqueness. This addresses the core issue of │
│ the in_bulk method failing when encountering │
│ UniqueConstraint fields.  The existing logic │
│ was implicitly assuming that all unique      │
│ fields had unique=True in the model          │
│ definition, which is not always the case.    │
│ This modification ensures that the           │
│ uniqueness check is performed correctly      │
│ regardless of whether the field is defined   │
│ with unique=True or a UniqueConstraint.      │
